{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If HaShem desires us.</b> They were cunning to speak in language of doubt, so that they would leave him alone to finish his words, for they would say that his words are merely hedging the possibility and not in the mode of certainty. Therefore they let him finish saying all his words, and when they were done they said to stone him. And here the question arises: why did they not stone him at the beginning of his words, since after all there is no addition or change in his latter words compared to the beginning of his words? Rather, it is because at the beginning of his words he said ״if,״ they were sitting and waiting for the conclusion of his words, and when he stood by them they said to stone him." "<b>A land which, etc.</b> Here is the cutting off of the statement ״If He desires.״" "<b>It flows with milk and honey.</b> The meaning of <b>it</b> is — and not another like it. And the spies said (Numbers 14:8) ״it flows with milk and honey — it״; the word ״it״ is not set apart from ״land״ to exclude the existence of its like, but rather for a reminder upon which the statement ״flows with milk and honey״ came."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:46.393708646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}